 <kendinikertenkelebek@me.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:59:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(build): skip architecture-bound build types, compare
 architectures by meaning

- Builder.get_build_types() drops packages whose build type is bound to
  another architecture: a <Package buildType="emul32"> (32-bit multilib)
  is not built on aarch64, with a message saying so. Recipe-specific build
  types such as zlib's minizip are still built everywhere, and
  ignored_build_types in pisi.conf works as before.
- <ExcludeArch> and the install-time architecture check compare through
  the table, so aliases (arm64, amd64) count.
- pisi emerge filters out sources excluded for the current architecture
  before planning, instead of stopping at the first excluded package of a
  component.

Tests (tests/archinfotest.py, 17 tests) cover the table, aliases,
exclusion, configuration defaults and the build-type selection with a
builder test double. They pass with Python 2.7 in pisilinux/chroot
(x86_64, emulated) and natively on arm64 (python:2.7 image, C extensions
stubbed). The other test modules give the same results as before the
change (utiltest, relationtest, archivetests and srcarchivetest already
failed on master).

Integration, with this PiSi installed in pisilinux/chroot:
- zlib as x86_64 produces the same five packages as stock PiSi (zlib,
  zlib-devel, zlib-32bit, minizip, minizip-devel);
- zlib with architecture = aarch64 skips zlib-32bit and produces
  aarch64-named packages;
- which with <ExcludeArch>arm64</ExcludeArch> refuses to build as aarch64;
- the emerge filter keeps which on x86_64 and drops it on aarch64.
---
 pisi/operations/build.py   |  14 ++-
 pisi/operations/emerge.py  |  22 +++++
 pisi/operations/install.py |   4 +-
 tests/archinfotest.py      | 172 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 210 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/archinfotest.py

diff --git a/pisi/operations/build.py b/pisi/operations/build.py
index 3892734..292bf71 100644
--- a/pisi/operations/build.py
+++ b/pisi/operations/build.py
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ import pisi.specfile
 import pisi.util as util
 import pisi.file
 import pisi.context as ctx
+import pisi.archinfo
 import pisi.dependency as dependency
 import pisi.api
 import pisi.sourcearchive
@@ -318,7 +319,8 @@ class Builder:
         """Build the package in one shot."""
 
         architecture = ctx.config.values.general.architecture
-        if architecture in self.spec.source.excludeArch:
+        # Aliases count too: <ExcludeArch>arm64</ExcludeArch> excludes aarch64.
+        if pisi.archinfo.excluded(architecture, self.spec.source.excludeArch):
             raise ExcludedArchitectureException(
                     _("pspec.xml avoids this package from building for '%s'")
                     % architecture)
@@ -358,6 +360,7 @@ class Builder:
     def get_build_types(self):
         ignored_build_types = \
                 ctx.config.values.build.ignored_build_types.split(",")
+        arch = pisi.archinfo.get(ctx.config.values.general.architecture)
         build_types = [""]
         packages = []
 
@@ -366,6 +369,15 @@ class Builder:
                 if package.buildType in ignored_build_types:
                     continue
 
+                # e.g. emul32 (32-bit multilib) only exists on x86_64; on
+                # other architectures those packages are simply not built,
+                # so recipes need no per-architecture conditionals for it.
+                if not arch.supports_build_type(package.buildType):
+                    ctx.ui.info(_("Skipping %s: build type '%s' is not "
+                                  "supported on %s") % (package.name,
+                                  package.buildType, arch.name))
+                    continue
+
                 if package.buildType not in build_types:
                     build_types.append(package.buildType)
 
diff --git a/pisi/operations/emerge.py b/pisi/operations/emerge.py
index 3701dd4..e560a4e 100644
--- a/pisi/operations/emerge.py
+++ b/pisi/operations/emerge.py
@@ -23,12 +23,34 @@ import pisi.util as util
 import pisi.atomicoperations as atomicoperations
 import pisi.ui as ui
 import pisi.db
+import pisi.db.sourcedb
+import pisi.archinfo
+
+def filter_excluded_architecture(A):
+    """Drop source packages whose <ExcludeArch> lists this architecture.
+
+    A component emerge (e.g. "kernel.drivers") would otherwise stop at the
+    first x86-only module on aarch64; excluded sources are reported and
+    skipped instead, the same way the farm skips them when building.
+    """
+    architecture = ctx.config.values.general.architecture
+    sourcedb = pisi.db.sourcedb.SourceDB()
+    kept = set()
+    for name in A:
+        if sourcedb.has_spec(name):
+            spec = sourcedb.get_spec(name)
+            if pisi.archinfo.excluded(architecture, spec.source.excludeArch):
+                ctx.ui.info(_("Skipping %s: excluded for %s") % (name, architecture))
+                continue
+        kept.add(name)
+    return kept
 
 def emerge(A):
 
     # A was a list, remove duplicates and expand components
     A = [str(x) for x in A]
     A_0 = A = pisi.operations.helper.expand_src_components(set(A))
+    A_0 = A = filter_excluded_architecture(A)
     ctx.ui.debug('A = %s' % str(A))
 
     if len(A)==0:
